---
import { releaseUrl, releaseVersion, installerSha256, windowsDownloadUrl, portableDownloadUrl, portableSize, androidDownloadUrl, androidReleaseUrl, androidUniversalUrl, androidUniversalSize } from '../config/product';
---

<section class="page-section faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <header class="section-head">
    <h2 id="faq-title">A few useful details.</h2>
  </header>
  <details>
    <summary>Which files can I read?</summary>
    <div class="details-body"><p>PDF, DRM-free reflowable EPUB, HTML, plain text and Markdown. <strong>Open</strong> (<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd>), a drop on the window or a double-click in Explorer reads the file where it is. <strong>Add</strong> (<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>I</kbd>) copies it into your library instead.</p></div>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>How are PDFs shown?</summary>
    <div class="details-body"><p>Two ways, and you can switch without losing your page. Document view keeps the original layout. Book view reflows the text into your reading theme; it needs a PDF text layer and does not perform OCR.</p></div>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>How does Listen work?</summary>
    <div class="details-body"><p>Select the Listen icon or press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>U</kbd>. simPl reads from the current page onward and marks the spoken word. To start somewhere else, right-click the text and choose <strong>Read aloud from here</strong>. It uses the voices installed in Windows, so it works offline.</p></div>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Which languages can I translate words between?</summary>
    <div class="details-body"><p>English ↔ Turkish, Spanish, German, French, Japanese and Chinese, plus Korean → English. Dictionaries are optional downloads, and lookups run on your computer. These are dictionary meanings, not sentence translations. See the <a href="/credits/">dictionary credits</a>.</p></div>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Can I highlight text and take notes?</summary>
    <div class="details-body"><p>Yes. Select text to highlight it or add a note, and right-click a page to bookmark it. <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>B</kbd> opens them all in a sidebar. Export them as Markdown, text or JSON from Settings › Library &amp; data.</p></div>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>How do I back up or move my library?</summary>
    <div class="details-body"><p>Open Settings › Library &amp; data. <strong>Create backup</strong> saves your settings, shelves, positions and notes in a ZIP, and optionally the books. <strong>Change…</strong> under Library folder moves your books to a folder you pick, for example on another drive.</p></div>
  </details>
  <details id="install">
    <summary>How do I install or update simPl?</summary>
    <div class="details-body"><p>Run the installer. To update, run the new one over the version you have; your library, notes and settings are kept. The installer is not code-signed yet, so if Windows SmartScreen appears, choose <strong>More info</strong>, then <strong>Run anyway</strong>.</p>{windowsDownloadUrl && installerSha256 && <p>SHA-256 of the {releaseVersion} installer, also in the <a href={releaseUrl}>release notes</a>:<br /><code class="hash">{installerSha256}</code></p>}{portableDownloadUrl && <p>Prefer not to install? Extract the <a href={portableDownloadUrl} download>portable ZIP</a> ({portableSize}) and run <strong>simPl.exe</strong>.</p>}{androidDownloadUrl && <p>On Android 8.0 or later, download the APK and allow installs from your browser when asked{androidUniversalUrl && <>. The <a href={androidUniversalUrl} download>universal APK</a> ({androidUniversalSize}) also supports x86_64 devices</>}. Checksums are in the <a href={androidReleaseUrl}>Android release notes</a>.</p>}</div>
  </details>
</section>
